"answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative led by Sarah Tan, with an initial budget of $500,000 (later adjusted to $550,000) and a kick-off scheduled for June 15th. Key developments include securing a strategic partnership with TechInnovate for AI research, expanding the team with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, and appointing Omar Jensen as lead developer for the development phase. The project has achieved several milestones, including the successful completion of the testing phase and the first major milestone (a secure file sharing prototype) ahead of schedule. Upcoming activities include an onboarding session on September 10th, UI enhancements planned for October, a celebration on October 10th, feedback collection by the end of November, and the implementation of updated security protocols (MFA and encryption) effective January next year."
